# EXPO_PUBLIC_-prefixed vars are the ONLY ones bundled into client JS by
# Expo — never rename these without the prefix, and never add a
# service-role/secret key here (spec section 24).
#
# Auth Slice C — Supabase is the identity provider ONLY (email + 6-digit
# OTP). The app never reads/writes data through Supabase (the project's
# Data API is disabled); athlete data goes only through the Vostivo API.
# Use the PUBLISHABLE key (`sb_publishable_...`, Supabase dashboard ->
# Project Settings -> API Keys). A secret (`sb_secret_...`) or legacy
# service_role key is refused at startup. Your real values live only in
# the gitignored .env — never commit them.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key

# The Plan/Workout API base URL this app talks to. No production
# deployment exists yet — this is required for local/native verification
# only.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:4000

# DEV/NATIVE-VERIFICATION ONLY — never set in a real build pipeline.
# A dev identity needs a non-production EXPO_PUBLIC_VOSTIVO_ENV. PRECEDENCE
# (non-production): a dev token below, when set, WINS over Supabase sign-in;
# with both dev tokens empty the app uses Supabase email OTP; with neither
# configured there is no session and the IdentityGate fails closed. Dev
# tokens are minted against the API's LOCAL JWKS — they do not verify while
# the API points at the cloud Supabase project (and vice versa). In
# production only Supabase is accepted. Setting a dev token
# while EXPO_PUBLIC_VOSTIVO_ENV is "production" (or unset) is a
# misconfiguration the app refuses to boot with, on purpose — see
# docs/domain/AUTH-LOCAL-ATHLETE-BOUNDARY-V1.md.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VOSTIVO_ENV=local
# One dev identity (also honoured by a non-production RELEASE build, for
# native verification). Mint with `pnpm --filter @vostivo/api auth:local:mint-jwt`.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_JWT=
# D-8 dev identity selector (only in a __DEV__ build): comma-separated
# `alias=jwt` pairs, e.g. `athlete-a=<jwt>,athlete-b=<jwt>`. Only the alias is
# ever shown on screen; real tokens live only in your gitignored .env.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_JWTS=
